{"name":"Rich Brocade","hex":"#925850","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rich","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Wealthy: having a lot of money and possessions.","Having an intense fatty or sugary flavour."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The rich people of a society or the world collectively, the rich class of a society.","(Can we verify this sense?)  the second placer in Tycoon"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rich"},{"term":"brocade","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A thick heavy fabric into which raised patterns have been woven, originally in gold and silver; more recently any cloth incorporating raised, woven patterns.","An item decorated with brocade."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To decorate fabric with raised woven patterns."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brocade"}],"entries":[{"title":"Brocade","blocks":[{"text":"Brocade is a class of richly decorative shuttle-woven fabrics, often made in coloured silks and sometimes with gold and silver threads. The name comes from Italian broccato meaning 'embossed cloth', originally past participle of the verb broccare 'to stud, set with nails', from brocco, 'small nail', from Latin broccus, 'projecting, pointed'."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Paris_-_Cath%C3%A9drale_Notre-Dame_-_Tr%C3%A9sor_de_la_cath%C3%A9drale_-_Ornements_sacerdotaux_-3.JPG/330px-Paris_-_Cath%C3%A9drale_Notre-Dame_-_Tr%C3%A9sor_de_la_cath%C3%A9drale_-_Ornements_sacerdotaux_-3.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brocade"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Brocart_de_soie_fran%C3%A7ais.jpg/250px-Brocart_de_soie_fran%C3%A7ais.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/86/Brocart_de_soie_fran%C3%A7ais.jpg?utm_source=en.wiki